  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine - Humanitarian - IOM 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the invasion of Ukraine on 24 February 2022, the humanitarian situation in the country quickly deteriorated. Ongoing attacks on Ukrainian energy and other vital infrastructure are expected to put millions of vulnerable conflict-affected people at higher risk during the upcoming winter season. Many of them live in damaged houses or buildings with insufficient access to heating or resources and/or markets to purchase winter essentials to keep warm. These conditions may force vulnerable populations into (further) displacement and/or affect their mental health and psychosocial well-being. Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to the protection of the most vulnerable populations (especially women and children) in Ukraine by mitigating the adverse impact of harsh weather conditions. IOM is implementing shelter activities; procuring generators for critical infrastructure; raising awareness on the availability of such initiatives as well as leading on data management with the displacement tracking matrix (DTM). In addition, IOM is also providing vulnerable population with access to functioning markets with multi-purpose cash assistance (MPCA), enabling families to address the variety of needs that may arise during the winter months.</narrative>
  </description>
